# Table

Use Table to display structured data. Columns can provide alignment, width, custom cells, and sorting. Choose `density="compact"` when space is limited.

Bind `selected` for row selection. The header checkbox selects only the rows passed to the table, so provide a stable `rowKey` or `getRowKey` when paginating. Sorting is controlled: bind `sortKey` and `sortDirection`, then reorder or fetch the rows yourself.

Use `copyable` for a row copy action, or `rowActions` for custom actions. For an interactive example, see [Data table](/docs/patterns/data-table).

<DocsExample title="Table" source={tableExampleSource} htmlSource={tableExampleHtmlSource}><TableExample /></DocsExample>

## Density

Choose a size for header and body rows. `default` = `lg`; `compact` = `sm`.

<DocsExample title="Table density" source={tableDensitySource} htmlSource={tableDensityHtmlSource}><TableDensityExample /></DocsExample>
